From b998d252b29d396b67a334806ea87a2d2082e8a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BRIGHT evolution experiment <experiment@local>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 15:24:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] aegis: add Tier-2 graded no-regression gate (continuous
 fitness)

Stock AEGIS gates reason only over binary per-task flags, and the only in-gate
regression check (counterfactual) compares final_output/exit_reason by exact
string equality on previously-passing tasks. On a graded metric a query can fall
from 0.62 to 0.21 while still passing a threshold, and the aggregate can rise at
the same time.

Adds gates/fitness.py: a frozen probe set is re-evaluated per candidate, requiring
  mean_fitness(candidate) >= mean_fitness(incumbent) + margin
  fitness_q(candidate)  >= fitness_q(incumbent) - delta   for every probe query
Context is threaded via AegisAgent(fitness_context=...) -> AegisOrchestrator ->
set_fitness_context(), mirroring set_counterfactual_context(). The gate runs LAST
(behind the cheap structural gates and the replay smoke test) because it is the
only gate that re-executes the harness, and it self-skips when no context is
wired, so GAIA/tau2/tb2 keep stock behaviour.
